109 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 51 0 R
/T (To build a fully functional task manager using only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript without any external frameworks. To allow users to add, view, update, and delete tasks seamlessly. To provide task categorization based on importance \(High, Medium, Low\) and difficulty \(Hard,  Medium, Easy\). To implement persistent data storage using browser localStorage so tasks survive page reloads. To display real-time statistics showing the count of Total, Pending, In Progress, and Done tasks. To provide filtering by task status and sorting by due date, importance, or difficulty. To visually indicate overdue and today-due tasks with color-coded labels. To deliver a clean, responsive, and intuitive user interface for all screen sizes.)
/E (To build a fully functional task manager using only HTML, CSS, and JavaScript without any external frameworks. To allow users to add, view, update, and delete tasks seamlessly. To provide task categorization based on importance \(High, Medium, Low\) and difficulty \(Hard,  Medium, Easy\). To implement persistent data storage using browser localStorage so tasks survive page reloads. To display real-time statistics showing the count of Total, Pending, In Progress, and Done tasks. To provide filtering by task status and sorting by due date, importance, or difficulty. To visually indicate overdue and today-due tasks with color-coded labels. To deliver a clean, responsive, and intuitive user interface for all screen sizes.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
